=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: `if: false` on an action that publishes pytest's results disables no suite
origin: issue #196 ruling 191.5 — a `uses:` step is a runner site only when one of its `with:` inputs names
origin2: a runner too. A publisher given a report path runs no tests. v0.5.0 blocked this diff as
origin3: "pmeier/pytest-results-action@v0 is disabled".
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest --junitxml=junit.xml
      - uses: pmeier/pytest-results-action@v0
        with:
          path: junit.xml
        if: always()
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest --junitxml=junit.xml
      - uses: pmeier/pytest-results-action@v0
        with:
          path: junit.xml
        if: false
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
